    "body": "## Description\n\n`PPOTrainer._save_hf` calls `Saver.save` for the actor and then for the critic in the same training step. Each call ran the shared `EpochStepTimeFreqCtl.check`, so the step and epoch counters advanced twice per step, and the time window was reset by the first call. As a result, when a critic is used:\n\n- `saver.freq_steps=2` (or `freq_epochs=2`): the critic is saved every step (or epoch) and the actor is never saved.\n- `saver.freq_secs=N`: the first call resets the window, so the actor is saved and the critic is not.\n\nThis PR makes the frequency decision once per global step in `Saver` and reuses it for the other models saved in that step. Trainers that save a single model behave exactly as before, and the saved `freq_ctl` state format is unchanged.\n\nReproduction (`freq_steps=2`, actor + critic saved each step, 6 steps):\n\n```\nbefore: actor saves at steps: []               critic saves at steps: ['0', '1', '2', '3', '4', '5']\nafter:  actor saves at steps: ['1', '3', '5']  critic saves at steps: ['1', '3', '5']\n```\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNone; no existing issue or PR covers it.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`)\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n## Additional Context\n\nAdded `test_save_applies_frequency_once_per_step_for_all_models` to `tests/test_saver.py`, parametrized over `freq_steps=2` and `freq_epochs=2`. It fails on `main` (the actor is never saved) and passes with this change. All of `tests/test_saver.py` passes (6 tests). `pre-commit run --files` on the two changed files passes (ruff lint/format, SPDX header). These are CPU-only unit tests; I did not run a full PPO training job.\n",
